WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.037
- Ryan Reaves suffered a brutal leg injury last week during a preseason game,

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:06.406
and all eyes are on his injury status.

00:00:06.423 --> 00:00:09.926
Here's why everyone wants to see him in the lineup on opening night.

00:00:09.926 --> 00:00:13.763
I'm Nasher here with B/R Open Ice, and today we're diving into the rivalry

00:00:13.763 --> 00:00:16.166
of the Rangers versus the Capitals.

00:00:16.166 --> 00:00:20.003
The two are set to face off on October 13, and this is shaping up to

00:00:20.003 --> 00:00:24.140
be an absolute battle. As you may or may not know, these teams, they

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:27.243
have some history. First, let's talk about Tom Wilson.

00:00:27.243 --> 00:00:31.197
On May 3, 2021, Tom Wilson caused chaos.

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:35.368
Buchnevich was down on the ice in the crease. Tom Wilson comes from behind

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:38.538
and pounds his head into the ice. As you can probably imagine, Rangers

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:42.509
players did not take too kindly to that, as Artemi Panarin comes into

00:00:42.509 --> 00:00:46.346
the mix, pulls Wilson off of Buchnevich and then takes him

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:49.682
on himself. Artemi Panarin, one of the best goal scorers and playmakers in

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:52.202
the league, had absolutely no chance.

00:00:52.202 --> 00:00:56.456
Eventually, Tom Wilson rag-dolls him around the ice, throws him down.

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:59.692
He hits his head a couple times without a helmet on.

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:01.761
It is just a terrible situation.

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:05.031
To make matters worse, Tom Wilson then heads to the penalty box, where he

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:09.085
flexes without a jersey on to the Rangers bench.

00:01:09.085 --> 00:01:12.188
Eventually resulted in him being kicked out of the game.

00:01:12.188 --> 00:01:16.443
This moment right here changed the course of New York Rangers history.

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:20.280
The Rangers ended up firing their GM and president, and now they were on

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:22.715
the hunt for a true enforcer.

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:24.484
That's where Ryan Reaves comes in.

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:28.505
Reaves is one of the last remaining true enforcers in the NHL.

00:01:28.505 --> 00:01:32.158
In 686 career NHL games played, he

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:35.728
has racked up 937 penalty minutes

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:37.597
and only 49 goals.

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:40.316
While you won't see a guy like Reaves on the scoreboard very often, he can

00:01:40.316 --> 00:01:44.821
easily turn the tides of a game with his energy, aggression and passion.

00:01:44.821 --> 00:01:48.024
You have to keep your head up or you're gettin' laid out.

00:01:48.024 --> 00:01:51.361
Not only is Reaves one of the toughest enforcers in the league already, he

00:01:51.361 --> 00:01:53.429
and Tom Wilson, they go way back.

00:01:53.429 --> 00:01:57.750
In 2013, back in Wilson's rookie season, after a big hit, Wilson

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:01.754
dropped the gloves with Reaves, and after a brief little wrestling match,

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:05.358
did tackle him down to the ice. Almost exactly a year later, the two would

00:02:05.358 --> 00:02:08.428
meet again, and this one was more than a wrestling match.

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:12.432
Reaves would connect on quite a few punches and drop Tom Wilson.

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:15.902
Over the course of the decade, Ryan Reaves would move from team to team, but

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:17.871
the rivalry still lived on.

00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:22.175
How can we ever forget the viral video of Reaves dropping Tom Wilson

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:24.761
twice in just eight seconds?

00:02:24.761 --> 00:02:28.598
There's some mutual respect between the two and also some vicious hatred,

00:02:28.598 --> 00:02:31.434
and that's what makes this rivalry so special.

00:02:31.434 --> 00:02:34.854
These two teams met in the playoffs four out of the last 10 years, most

00:02:34.854 --> 00:02:38.942
notably in 2013, where King Lundqvist shut the Capitals out

00:02:38.942 --> 00:02:41.511
in Game 6 and 7 to advance.

00:02:41.511 --> 00:02:44.881
We can only hope that Reaves makes it into the lineup on opening night, but

00:02:44.881 --> 00:02:48.484
regardless, this will be a battle of the ages.

00:02:48.484 --> 00:02:52.105
I'm Nasher here with B/R Open Ice. Let's see what happens.

